# Paths excluded from compile-db coverage, one git pathspec per line, with `#`
# for a comment.
#
# List a directory here only when another build owns it, so that its sources are
# absent from this tree's compile database. Linting them would run clang-tidy on
# invented flags. Do not list code that this build compiles, which must be
# linted. The listing is not a suppression, because the project that owns the
# sources still compiles them with warnings as errors.
#
# The compile-db coverage check reads this file. Lint enumerates compile
# commands, so these sources are absent from its inputs. Every tracked
# translation unit is either linted or declared absent here with a written
# reason.

# The installed-package consumer (tests/consumer) is a separate CMake project
# configured against an installed pico_util and built by the `consumer` gate.
# This tree's build never references it, so its translation unit is in neither
# half of the merged compile database.
tests/consumer/*

